\mycircled{0} The mass of KCl your weighted, $m$.\vspace{0.5cm}\\
\mycircled{1} The average activity in cpm.\vspace{0.5cm}\\
\mycircled{2} The standard deviation in cps for the background ($s_b$) and the background+sample ($s_{b+s}$). For the sample ($s_s$), you need to use: $s_s=\sqrt{s_{b+s}^2-s_{s}^2}$  \vspace{0.5cm}\\
\mycircled{3} These are the activity values in cpm for the background (without K).\vspace{0.5cm}\\
\mycircled{4} These are the activity values in cpm for the sample.\vspace{0.5cm}\\
\mycircled{5} These are the activity values in cpm for the sample without the background. You can subtract the average value and the standard deviation.
